<script type="text/javascript">
    var initial_state = {
        pType: "algorithm",
        slug: "turn-off-lights-be46dc6c",
        title: "Turn Off Lights",
        topicTree: {"track": {"url": "/practice/algorithms/", "title": "Algorithms"}, "topic": {"url": "/practice/algorithms/string-algorithm/", "title": "String Algorithms"}, "sub_topic": {"url": "/practice/algorithms/string-algorithm/string-searching/", "title": "String Searching"}},
        problemData: {"id": 2803272, "title": "Turn Off Lights", "description": "<p>There are&nbsp;<em><span class=\"mathjax-latex\">\\(n\\)</span></em>&nbsp;bulbs arranged in a row. The state of the bulbs is represented by a binary string&nbsp;<em>bulbs</em> of length&nbsp;<em><span class=\"mathjax-latex\">\\(n\\)</span></em>, the&nbsp;<em><span class=\"mathjax-latex\">\\(0\\)</span></em>&nbsp;at&nbsp;<em><span class=\"mathjax-latex\">\\(i^{th}\\)</span>&nbsp;</em>position&nbsp;in the string represents the bulb is OFF and&nbsp;<em><span class=\"mathjax-latex\">\\(1\\)</span></em>&nbsp;represents the bulb is ON, where <span class=\"mathjax-latex\">\\(0 \\leq\u00a0i &lt; n\\)</span>. You have to switch OFF all the bulbs by performing following operation atmost&nbsp;<em><span class=\"mathjax-latex\">\\(k\\)</span></em>&nbsp;times. The operation is defined as:-</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Choose any index&nbsp;<em><span class=\"mathjax-latex\">\\(i\\)</span></em>&nbsp;in the string&nbsp;<em>bulb</em>&nbsp;and turn OFF all the lights having indexes&nbsp;<em><span class=\"mathjax-latex\">\\(i\\)</span>&nbsp;</em>to&nbsp;<span class=\"mathjax-latex\">\\(\\min(n - 1, i + l - 1)\\)</span><em> </em>(inclusive), where&nbsp;<em><span class=\"mathjax-latex\">\\(l\\)</span></em>&nbsp;is a pre defined number, greater than zero and fixed for all the operations.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>The task is to find the smallest value of&nbsp;<em><span class=\"mathjax-latex\">\\(l\\)</span></em>&nbsp;greater than zero, such that you can turn OFF all the bulbs in atmost&nbsp;<em><span class=\"mathjax-latex\">\\(k\\)</span></em>&nbsp;operations.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Input format</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>The first line of input contains two space separated integers,&nbsp;<em><span class=\"mathjax-latex\">\\(n\\)</span></em>&nbsp;and <em><span class=\"mathjax-latex\">\\(k\\)</span></em>, representing the size of string&nbsp;<em>bulb&nbsp;</em>and maximum number of operations you can perform.</li>\n\t<li>The second line of input contains a binary string,&nbsp;<em>bulbs.</em></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>Output format</strong></p>\n\n<p>The output contains a single integer, the minimum possible value of&nbsp;<em><em><span class=\"mathjax-latex\">\\(l\\)</span></em></em>&nbsp;greater than zero&nbsp;such that you are able to turn OFF all the bulbs in atmost&nbsp;<em><span class=\"mathjax-latex\">\\(k\\)</span></em>&nbsp;operations.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Constraints</strong></p>\n\n<p><strong><span class=\"mathjax-latex\">\\(1 \\leq n \\leq 10^6 \\\\ 1 \\leq k \\leq n\\)</span></strong></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>", "sample_explanation": "<p>For&nbsp;<em>l&nbsp;</em>= 1, The operation can be perfomed by choosing following intervals</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>[1, 1], [3, 3], [5, 5], [6, 6], [7, 7], [8, 8], [9, 9] - 7 operations</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>For&nbsp;<em>l&nbsp;</em>= 2, The operation can be perfomed by choosing following intervals</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>[1, 2], [3, 4], [5, 6], [7, 8], [9, 9] - 5 operations</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>For&nbsp;<em>l&nbsp;</em>= 3, The operation can be perfomed by choosing following intervals</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>[1, 3], [5, 7], [8, 9] - 3 operations</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Hence the answer is 3.</p>", "tags": "String Algorithms,Algorithms,String Searching", "level": "M", "private_url_hash": "29b99bf104974d4caeb577614ada0224", "ratings": {"score": 4.4, "votes": 8}, "success_rate": 78, "points": 30, "attempted_by": 2131, "bookmarked": false, "time_limit": 5.0, "memory_limit": 256, "max_code_size": 1024, "editorial": {"state": "unlocked"}},
        activeTab: "description",
        baseURL: "/practice/algorithms/string-algorithm/string-searching/practice-problems/algorithm/turn-off-lights-be46dc6c/",
        isSourceList: false,
        shareURL: "https://www.hackerearth.com/practice/algorithms/string-algorithm/string-searching/practice-problems/algorithm/turn-off-lights-be46dc6c/"
    }
    
